{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "label": "managementRoutes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Baut einen Route-Baum betrieblicher Endpunkte und gibt ihn zurueck \u2014 sonst nichts. Der Aufrufer bindet ihn, ueblicherweise auf Port 8558; cluster ist optional (null ueberspringt /cluster/*)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutesoptions", "label": "ManagementRoutesOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "enableLeaveEndpoint, enableDownEndpoint, enableMetricsEndpoint, auth, ipAllowlist und authProtectHealth. Port und Host sind keine Settings \u2014 sie gehen an system.http(port, { host }), und cluster ist das zweite positionale Argument."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_separate_management_port", "label": "Warum ein separater Port", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die Endpunkte legen internen Zustand offen (Mitgliederadressen, Metrikwerte); auf einem eigenen, intern gefirewallten Port zu binden trennt sie vom oeffentlichen App-Port. In K8s ist das per-Pod \u2014 Probes treffen :8558 vom Kubelet, kein Service exponiert es extern."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_k8s_probe_integration", "label": "K8s-Probe-Integration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "readinessProbe auf /ready und livenessProbe auf /health; K8s pollt sie, um zu entscheiden, ob der Pod Traffic bekommt oder neu gestartet wird."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_mount_into_existing_server", "label": "In einen bestehenden Server mounten", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "managementRoutes gibt schlichte Routen zurueck, die sich per concat in bestehende App-Routen haengen lassen \u2014 sinnvoll, wenn schon ein HTTP-Server existiert oder eine Single-Node-App den Extra-Port nicht rechtfertigt. Auf dem oeffentlichen Port exponiert das internen Zustand erneut und gehoert dann gegated."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutesoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_k8s_probe_integration", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_separate_management_port", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "sou